															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/zyn" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1404533); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1404533&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1605928873" alt="Zyn" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1404533)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/zyn" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1404533); return false;" >Zyn</a></span> <span class="odate time_1602740274 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">15 Oct 2020 05:37</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4795972">
									

<p>Due to the ever-increasing demand for more skilled reviewers to help out in the forums, the Forum Criticism Staff Team has been holding 2-week mentoring periods to train up-and-coming reviewers. These are known as &quot;Flights&quot;.</p>
<p><strong>What does being part of a Flight mean?</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Flight 1 will run from November 1 to November 15. Flight 2 will run from November 15 to November 31.</li>
<li>Experienced reviewer mentors (dubbed &quot;commanders&quot;) will work with mentees (&quot;officers&quot;) in the Writing Help forums to critique concepts and drafts while the officers practice and improve their critique skills.</li>
<li>At the start of the Flight, officers will determine their weekly goals for two categories: activity and quality. Activity can be something simple like &quot;crit at least one thread a day&quot;, quality something like &quot;be more familiar with matching authors to helpful resources/guides/example articles&quot;. Commanders will discuss these goals weekly.</li>
<li>Officers will be taught some forum management skills like how to respond (without backseat modding) to a thread that breaks guidelines.</li>
<li>If the officers cannot yet greenlight, they may officially recommend concepts to their commander for greenlight consideration.</li>
<li>Flight teams can have funny/rule of cool names. Commander discretion.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Who are the commanders this month?</strong></p>
<p>The commander for Flight 1 is <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/karakatt" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5950867); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5950867&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1603151472" alt="KaraKatt" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5950867)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/karakatt" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5950867); return false;">KaraKatt</a></span>.</p>
<p>The commanders for Flight 2 are <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/nagiros" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4665703); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4665703&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1603151472" alt="Nagiros" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4665703)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/nagiros" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4665703); return false;">Nagiros</a></span>, <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/truc-linh" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5813515); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5813515&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1603151472" alt="Truc Linh" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5813515)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/truc-linh" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5813515); return false;">Truc Linh</a></span>, and <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/zyn" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1404533); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1404533&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1603151472" alt="Zyn" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1404533)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/zyn" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1404533); return false;">Zyn</a></span>.</p>
<p><strong>Who can request consideration to be an officer?</strong></p>
<p>Anyone! Newbies and veterans alike are welcome to put their names forth.</p>
<p><strong>What do Flight participants get at the end?</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>For as long as the mentorship system continues, <em>Flight teams will select the featured SCP, tale, and GoI format</em> displayed on the front page of the site. Flight team member names will also be displayed on the front page of the site.<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-984959-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-984959-1')">1</a></sup></li>
<li><em>Officers deemed ready by their commanders will be given greenlighting privileges</em> (if they do not have them already), and their names and number of successful Flights will be displayed on the <a href="/butterfly-squad-roster">Butterfly Squad Roster</a>.</li>
<li>(Remember, provision of the rewards is up to commander discretion!)</li>
</ul>
<div class="footnotes-footer">
<div class="title">Footnotes</div>
<div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-984959-1"><a href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnoteref-984959-1')">1</a>. To accommodate up to six teams, the number of potential monthly front page features will be doubled.</div>
</div>

